<title>USA: U.S. 14-day bill auction average rate 5.25 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 14-day bill auction average rate 5.25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its auction of 14-day cash management bills brought these results:</p>
<p>14-DAY BILLS DUE JUNE 17, 1997 * $30.022 BILLION</p>
<p>	  DISCOUNT	    INVESTMENT	    PRICE</p>
<p>	  BID RANGE	     RATE		  RANGE</p>
<p>     LOW  5.23		  5.31		 99.797</p>
<p>    HIGH  5.28		  5.36		 99.795</p>
<p> AVERAGE  5.25		  5.33		 99.796</p>
<p>TOTAL BIDS $64.243 BLN OR 2.14 TIMES AMOUNT SOLD</p>
<p>		     AWARDED AT HIGH DISCOUNT: 69 PCT</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 17.Jun.97</p>
